      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "H3 VIDEO STILL STUDIO 2026-11-11.1\n\nThe MODEL dropdown changes only one selected backend, not three simultaneous runs.\nAuto video: MiniMax/Eros receive native reference video; P-H3 receives source-file keyframes. Keyframes for all engines is useful for a controlled comparison.\nActive photo slots are numbered consecutively. Video keyframes are appended after the active photos. <Video 1> is expanded to their Picture tags on keyframe routes. Read the reference report.\nStandard H3: 50 steps, no Turbo. Eros Fix1: 8 steps, baked Turbo, 12/3 shift. P-H3: fixed native 8-step schedule. No prompt enhancer, Spark, Spectrum, VSA or automatic upscaler.\nPhoto/image cap is independent of output MP. Video crop is applied before downscaling. P-H3 has 8 TOTAL image slots, including video keyframes; H3/Eros have 9. No inputs are silently discarded.\nStart at 2.5 MP for video H3/Eros, then compare 4 MP. Try 8 MP only after checking VRAM. P-H3 uses 4 MP here; 8 MP is optional.\nBF16 files are optional: python3 /opt/h3-still/video_studio/manage.py download bf16 . Use only with applicable model authorization. No model weights are in this JSON.\nPreserved Lab workflows provide SAM, reference crops and RefMods. Accelerator experiments remain separate.\nBackground protection requires a painted target mask and composites ORIGINAL pixels outside it. It does not guide diffusion. It can leave remnants if the replacement pose leaves the mask.\nFactory files never overwrite saved user copies. Save your edited workflow under a personal name.\nNo GPU inference has been run by the package author in this environment. Validate one engine at a time.\n\nPowered by MiniMax H3. Check LICENSE_NOTES.md before use."
      ]
    }
